someone persuing the program), the program should core dump.  Same if
some of the data files are not yet decrypted.   When the program is
actually in use, it should delete all its data files after opening
them, so if the process is killed, the administrator cannot get to the
data file.  And, of course, the data should be internally managed in
such a way that doing a 'strings' on the coredump won't find it.  

Extra points if the program can accomplish the class assignment while
cracking the passwords :-)
