universities (para. 13), and that "[n]obody really cares" what we tell
other students (para. 14).

Many students applying to top schools may be mislead into thinking that
they will be taught by big-name Nobel Laureates, etc., and in that case,
the schools are being dishonest in their glossy brochures.  But the
important thing is that the students receive quality education, not
